# AAM imm8: ASCII adjust AX after multiply (Intel SDM pseudocode, 386).
# AH = AL / imm8 and AL = AL mod imm8. A zero imm8 is a divide error (#DE):
# the instruction faults and changes nothing. SF, ZF and PF follow the new
# AL; OF, AF and CF are undefined. Bound to AX by the decoder; the decoder
# replaces the base read with the instruction's immediate byte.
read ax dst 16
trunc al ax 8
read base src 8
zero base_zero base
not base_ok base_zero
require base_ok
div q al base
rem r al base
zext q_wide q 16
zext r_wide r 16
const shift 16 8
shl high q_wide shift
or result high r_wide
write dst result
bit sf r 7
zero zf r
parity pf r
flag SF sf
flag ZF zf
flag PF pf
undef_flag OF
undef_flag AF
undef_flag CF
retire
